+# Rigging
+
+## Stack
+
+- language: JavaScript
+- runtime: none
+- packageManager: npm
+
+## Directories
+
+- implementation: .
+- specs: features
+- verification: none
+- assets: assets
+- scantlings: none
+
+## Commands
+
+- discover: none
+- prove: `ref="{scenario}"; npx cucumber-js "${ref%%:*}" --name "^${ref#*:}$" --tags "not @captain and not @shipwright"`
+- sweep: none
+- coverage: none
+- step-usage: none
+- plank-inventory: none
+- typecheck: none
+- lint: none
+- conformance: none
+
+## Perturbation
+
+- message: `PERTURBATION: consider current durable context; remove when fixed`
+- perturb: `throw new Error("PERTURBATION: consider current durable context; remove when fixed");`
+
+## Tiers
+
+- default: none
+- sandbox: none
+- policy: none
+- weather: none
+- runrecord: none
+
+## Dependencies
+
+- policy: locked
+- dependency: @cucumber/cucumber
+- dependency: happy-dom
+
+## Outbound
+
+- outbound: none
diff --git a/features/todo-counter-and-filters.feature b/features/todo-counter-and-filters.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5fbcbd5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-counter-and-filters.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,107 @@
+Feature: Todo counter and filters
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many todos remain and filter by status
+  So that I can focus on relevant tasks
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: No todos
+
+    Scenario: Main and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+      Then the main section is hidden
+      And the footer section is hidden
+
+  Rule: Active todo counter
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows the number of active todos
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+        | Clean house  | false     |
+      Then the counter displays "2 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter uses singular form for one item
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      Then the counter displays "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows zero for no active items
+      Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      Then the counter displays "0 items left"
+
+  Rule: Clear completed button
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed removes all completed todos
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user clicks the clear-completed button
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" no longer exists
+      And the todo "Walk the dog" still exists
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no todos are completed
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when at least one todo is completed
+      Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      Then the clear-completed button is visible
+
+  Rule: Filter routing
+
+    Scenario: All filter shows all todos
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then both todos are visible
+
+    Scenario: Active filter shows only active todos
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then only the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+
+    Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then only the todo "Buy milk" is visible
+
+    Scenario: Active filter link is selected when viewing active todos
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then the filter link "Active" is selected
+
+    Scenario: Completed filter link is selected when viewing completed todos
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then the filter link "Completed" is selected
+
+    Scenario: All filter link is selected by default
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then the filter link "All" is selected
+
+    Scenario: Checking a todo while on active filter hides it from the list
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      And the user toggles the checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+      Then only the todo "Walk the dog" is visible
+
+  Rule: Main and footer visibility with todos
+
+    Scenario: Main and footer are visible when there are todos
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      Then the main section is visible
+      And the footer section is visible
diff --git a/features/todo-lifecycle.feature b/features/todo-lifecycle.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4910455
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-lifecycle.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,112 @@
+Feature: Todo lifecycle
+  As a user
+  I want to create, complete, edit, and remove todos
+  So that I can manage my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: New todos
+
+    Scenario: Creating a todo from input text
+      When the user types "Buy milk" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then a todo with title "Buy milk" exists in the list
+      And the new-todo input is empty
+
+    Scenario: Input is trimmed before creating a todo
+      When the user types "  Buy milk  " in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then a todo with title "Buy milk" exists in the list
+
+    Scenario: Empty or whitespace-only input creates no todo
+      When the user types "   " in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then the todo list is empty
+
+    Scenario: New todo input is focused on page load
+      Then the new-todo input has focus
+
+  Rule: Marking todos as complete
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the checkbox marks a todo as completed
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user toggles the checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+
+    Scenario: Unchecking a completed todo makes it active again
+      Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user toggles the checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" does not have the completed class
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all checks all todos
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then all todos are completed
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all unchecks when all are already complete
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | true      |
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then all todos are active
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle-all reflects state when a single todo is checked
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Rule: Destroying a todo
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the destroy button removes the todo
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user destroys the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" no longer exists
+
+  Rule: Editing a todo
+
+    Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label activates editing mode
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is in editing mode
+      And the edit input for "Buy milk" has focus
+
+    Scenario: Editing and confirming with Enter saves the new title
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input and presses Enter
+      Then a todo with title "Buy oat milk" exists in the list
+      And the todo "Buy milk" no longer exists
+
+    Scenario: Editing and confirming with blur saves the new title
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input and presses Enter on blur
+      Then a todo with title "Buy oat milk" exists in the list
+
+    Scenario: Editing with Escape discards changes
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "Changed" in the edit input and presses Escape
+      Then a todo with title "Buy milk" exists in the list
+      And the todo "Changed" does not exist
+
+    Scenario: Editing to empty text destroys the todo
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" no longer exists
+
+    Scenario: Editing is not persisted as an editing class
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the label of todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" has the editing class
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" does not have the editing class
diff --git a/features/todo-persistence.feature b/features/todo-persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..168f1dd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+Feature: Todo persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to survive page reloads
+  So that I don't lose my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: LocalStorage persistence
+
+    Scenario: Todos survive a page reload
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | true      |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then a todo with title "Buy milk" exists in the list
+      And a todo with title "Walk the dog" exists in the list
+
+    Scenario: Completed state survives a page reload
+      Given a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+
+    Scenario: Todos are persisted to localStorage under todos-vanilla
+      Given a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      Then the localStorage key "todos-vanilla" contains an array with 1 item
+      And the first item in localStorage "todos-vanilla" has title "Buy milk"
+
+    Scenario: New todo ID increments
+      Given the following todos exist:
+        | title        | completed |
+        | Buy milk     | false     |
+        | Walk the dog | false     |
+      Then the first item in localStorage "todos-vanilla" has id 1
+      And the second item in localStorage "todos-vanilla" has id 2
